## Project Idea

The main idea behind developing the **Ice Cream Parlour Management System** is to convert the day-to-day operations of an ice cream parlour into a simple, organized, and efficient digital system.

In a traditional parlour, activities such as managing menu items, checking stock, processing customer orders, calculating bills, and maintaining sales records may be handled manually. This can consume time and may lead to errors in billing, inventory management, and record maintenance.

This project brings these activities together in one application using Core Java, JDBC, and MySQL. It also incorporates the **Data Access Object (DAO) design pattern** to separate database operations from the main application logic, making the code more modular, reusable, and easier to maintain.

The system provides separate modules for customers and administrators. Customers can browse menu items, place orders, and receive bills, while administrators can manage menu items, update stock, and access relevant records.

