## DAO Concept in the Project

The DAO (Data Access Object) layer is responsible for handling database-related operations separately from the main application classes.

- `AdminDAO.java` — handles administrator authentication-related database operations.
- `MenuCategoryDAO.java` — manages menu category data.
- `MenuItemDAO.java` — handles menu item insertion, retrieval, updating, searching, and deletion.
- `OrderDAO.java` — manages customer orders, order details, and related stock operations.
- `BillDAO.java` — handles bill creation and retrieval.

The application uses `DBConnecton.java` to establish a JDBC connection to the existing MySQL database. The DAO classes use this connection to execute the required database operations.

